{"id":"R0014","key":"mobility_continuity","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Cluster-head disconnection and recovery were tested on the airborne-computer testbed; no outdoor UAV fault or mobility test was reported.","l":[[13,"VIII.C Performance of Elastic Efficient Scheduler","communication of one cluster head is cut off"]],"g":"Fault recovery tested only by cutting cluster-head communication on the airborne-computer testbed, not during outdoor UAV flight."}
{"id":"R0014","key":"optimization","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Two-layer heuristic load balancing equalizes predicted latency across clusters and within clusters, paired with adaptive intermediate-data quantization and compression.","l":[[6,"IV.A Inter-Cluster Load Balancing","maximize the computing efficiency in the cluster"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0014","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"ASAP lowers inference latency versus offloading and terrestrial baselines, cuts per-node compute and memory overhead, and reschedules within one second.","l":[[12,"VIII.B Overall Performance","reduces the computing and memory overhead per node"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0036","key":"architecture","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Server-driven edge analytics architecture where UAVs sample and upload video chunks to an edge server running profiling and configuration control.","l":[[5,"III.A System Model","schedule the UAVs for video chunk uploading"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0036","key":"code_data","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Uses the public ETH pedestrian detection dataset; no source code repository or custom dataset release is reported.","l":[[10,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","captured from a stereo rig mounted on car"]],"g":"No source code or implementation repository is released; only the external ETH dataset is cited."}
{"id":"R0036","key":"compute_radio","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Modeled in simulation via shared uplink bandwidth and edge FPS capacity without specifying physical radio or compute hardware.","l":[[12,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","network bandwidth and the computing capacity"]],"g":"Simulation-only bandwidth and FPS capacity parameters are used; physical UAV compute and radio hardware are not specified."}
{"id":"R0036","key":"limitations","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Evaluated on ground-view car-mounted video; authors note future need for spatiotemporal frame correlation and 3D aerial scene dynamics.","l":[[13,"VII. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE WORK","exploit 3D scene dynamics unique to aerial perspectives"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0036","key":"mobility_continuity","s":"NOT_REPORTED","f":"UAV flight mobility trajectories, link handovers, and node-failure continuity mechanisms are not modeled or evaluated.","l":[[11,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION",null]],"g":"No UAV mobility model, trajectory update, or fault/disconnection continuity mechanism is reported."}
{"id":"R0036","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"In ground-view-fed simulations, SAC2 outperforms baselines in effective surveillance coverage and maintains steadier accuracy under dynamic scenes.","l":[[11,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","outperforms baselines in effective coverage while significantly reducing"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0036","key":"variability","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Only the random-upload baseline reports 20-trial mean results; full-system variance or confidence intervals for SAC2 are not reported.","l":[[12,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","repeat 20 trials on each parameter setting"]],"g":"Twenty-trial averaging is reported only for the Random-to-upload baseline; variance or dispersion metrics for SAC2 are omitted."}
{"id":"R0036","key":"workload","s":"OBSERVED","f":"YOLOv5 object detection on 10-second chunks from the ground-view car-mounted ETH pedestrian dataset across multiple resolutions and frame rates.","l":[[10,"VI. PERFORMANCE EVALUATION","runs a YOLOv5 object detection model"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0038","key":"baselines","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Compared only against an unsplit complete model for accuracy and an uninterrupted run for latency; no external distributed baselines.","l":[[5,"V.B Experimental Results","ran as a complete model together"]],"g":"Evaluated against a centralized complete model and normal uninterrupted execution, with no experimental comparison to external distributed-inference baselines."}
{"id":"R0038","key":"limitations","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Benchtop-only evaluation over short distances without real UAV flight, plus minor accuracy drop and inconsistent end-to-end latency sum.","l":[[5,"V.B Experimental Results","short physical distance between the participating devices"]],"g":"Authors note only future multi-swarm replication; benchtop-only testing, missing flight evaluation, and the 108 ms vs 153 ms sum discrepancy are unaddressed."}
{"id":"R0038","key":"mobility_continuity","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Deliberate benchtop disconnection triggers pause, 40-second container redeployment, and Redis checkpoint restore; no UAV mobility or field testing occurred.","l":[[5,"V.B Experimental Results","device was intentionally removed from the swarm"]],"g":"Fault continuity tested via deliberate benchtop disconnection and Redis checkpoint restore, without physical UAV mobility or outdoor field trials."}
{"id":"R0038","key":"outcomes","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Distributed stages execute and recover from checkpoints without data loss, though reported aggregate latency is internally inconsistent with stage sums.","l":[[5,"V.B Experimental Results","continued processing from the previous checkpoint"]],"g":"Stage-level execution and checkpoint recovery are shown qualitatively, but the reported 108 ms total contradicts the 33, 45, 45, 30 ms stage sum."}
{"id":"R0038","key":"variability","s":"NOT_REPORTED","f":"No standard deviation, confidence intervals, or multi-run variance metrics are reported for latency or recovery time.","l":[[5,"V.B Experimental Results",null]],"g":"Only single-run averages over 100 images and an accuracy range are reported; variance and dispersion metrics are absent."}
{"id":"R0043","key":"compute_radio","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Simulated MANET with 20 MHz bandwidth, 10 dBm user transmit power, Rayleigh fading, 30 user UAVs, and six 60-GFLOPS server nodes.","l":[[5,"IV.A Simulation Setup","all server nodes have the same computing power"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0043","key":"evaluation","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Simulation-only evaluation comparing DIA against Random fusion, Random offload, and Greedy across four DNN benchmarks up to 3,000 tasks.","l":[[5,"IV.A Simulation Setup","Table 1 shows the parameters used in the simulation"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0043","key":"optimization","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Combines DIA-FP iterative fusion-block partitioning with DIA-O genetic-algorithm overlapping coalition formation to minimize maximum coalition inference latency.","l":[[4,"III.B Offloading Strategy Based on DIA-O","overlapping coalition formation algorithm based on genetic algorithm"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0043","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"In simulation, DIA achieves the lowest total inference time across all four DNNs, running 1.2x to 2.9x faster than baselines.","l":[[5,"IV.B Experiment Result","reaches the minimum value in all cases"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0043","key":"partition_assignment","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Groups convolutional layers into spatially split fusion sub-blocks with receptive-field overlap and assigns sub-tasks to server UAVs via binary matching.","l":[[4,"III.A Partitioning Strategy Based on DIA-FP","best partition scheme for this DNN model"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0043","key":"workload","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Maritime ship-detection visual workload from the SeaShip dataset using NiN, VGG16, AlexNet, and ResNet18 under Poisson task arrivals.","l":[[5,"IV.A Simulation Setup","data set covers six common ship types"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"access","s":"READ","f":"Original body page directly opened.","l":[[19,"6.1. Simulation settings","integrates ground edge servers with aerial UAV nodes"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"architecture","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Decentralized UAV-to-ground edge-server offloading architecture where UAVs bid for ground base-station server resources without a central coordinator.","l":[[5,"3.1. Inference offloading model","offloaded to edge servers within communication range"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"baselines","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Compares DADAO against four baselines: Local-only execution, MWBS double auction, LADPO cross-entropy optimization, and OATS online auction.","l":[[19,"6.1. Simulation settings","relying entirely on onboard computing resources"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"code_data","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Uses public CIFAR-10 test images for task generation; no source code or simulation script repository is reported.","l":[[19,"6.1. Simulation settings","randomly drawn from the test set"]],"g":"No source code repository is provided; only the public CIFAR-10 dataset is named."}
{"id":"R0058","key":"compute_radio","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Models 5G NR sub-6 GHz links at 1 MHz and 1–5 GHz servers; prose reports inconsistent 5–10 versus default 3 servers.","l":[[19,"6.1. Simulation settings","communication coverage radius of each edge server"]],"g":"Section 6.1 states 5-10 fixed edge servers with a contradictory default value of 3; actual default server count is unresolved."}
{"id":"R0058","key":"mobility_continuity","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Enforces remaining connection-time constraints under 3–13 m/s UAV mobility and handles link loss via higher-bid retries, buffering, or local fallback.","l":[[10,"4.1. Overview of UAV inference offloading process","retries offloading in the next round"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"optimization","s":"OBSERVED","f":"One-round distributed uniform-price auction with bidder payment verification that optimizes latency-accuracy utility in polynomial time while preserving truthfulness.","l":[[11,"4.2. Offloading problem modeling and bidding objectives","maximize the overall system utility"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"In simulation, DADAO achieves higher accuracy, lower latency, and higher task success rates under mobility than all compared baselines.","l":[[20,"6.2. Comparison of inference latency and accuracy","consistently maintains the lowest latency"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"partition_assignment","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Binary full-task offloading assigns each UAV task to at most one edge server per slot without DNN layer partitioning.","l":[[9,"3.4. Problem formulation","assigned to only one server per time slot"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0058","key":"variability","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Boxplots report task-success-rate distributions across UAV speeds; latency and accuracy plots report point values without variance metrics.","l":[[21,"6.3. Performance evaluation in dynamic environments","distribution of task success rates"]],"g":"Distribution boxplots are given for task success rate across speeds, but latency and accuracy results lack variance or confidence intervals."}
{"id":"R0064","key":"architecture","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Air-ground multi-UAV surveillance architecture with compressed DNNs onboard UAVs and uncompressed DNNs on ground edge servers via binary offloading.","l":[[4,"3. System model and problem formulation","uncompressed DNN model is deployed at ESs"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0064","key":"compute_radio","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Simulated probabilistic LoS/NLoS air-ground links at 2 MHz with 3 GHz UAVs and 15–20 GHz ground edge servers.","l":[[5,"3.3.2. Edge offloading","communication energy consumed by UAV"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0064","key":"mobility_continuity","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Optimizes 3D UAV trajectories with 50 m collision avoidance; node dropouts, packet loss, and mobile targets are not modeled.","l":[[4,"3.1.1. UAV mobility model","avoid collision between any two UAVs"]],"g":"3D flight mobility and collision avoidance are modeled, but link/node failure continuity and packet loss are omitted."}
{"id":"R0064","key":"optimization","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Centralized-training, distributed-execution MAPPO-HA decouples continuous 3D trajectory control from discrete frame sampling and binary offloading without action-space relaxation.","l":[[7,"4.2. MAPPO-HA algorithm","solve the hybrid action space without approximation"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0064","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"In simulation, MAPPO-HA achieves the lowest inference delay across bandwidth, server-capacity, and accuracy regimes while satisfying sensing and accuracy constraints.","l":[[9,"5.2.2. Impact of communication bandwidth","achieves the lowest inference delay"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0064","key":"variability","s":"PARTIAL","f":"Training fixes a single random seed rather than independent reruns; evaluation reports 50-episode averages and 95% confidence intervals across bandwidths.","l":[[9,"5.1. Simulation setup","random seeds are fixed in the simulations"],[9,"5.2.2. Impact of communication bandwidth","run the trained model for 50 episodes"]],"g":"Evaluation reports 50-episode test confidence intervals and shaded training curves, but training uses one fixed seed without independent multi-seed reruns."}
{"id":"R0064","key":"workload","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Analytical multi-frame video-recognition workload at 1080x1080 resolution with 5–20 frames and a fitted accuracy curve, without real video execution.","l":[[8,"5.1. Simulation setup","input size of one video frame"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0075","key":"architecture","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Master-Assistant multi-exit collaborative inference: Assistants extract and transmit early-exit features over wireless links for Master-side concatenation fusion and prediction.","l":[[4,"III.A Task Definition","one Master UAV and multiple Assistant UAVs"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0075","key":"optimization","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Validation-learned, test-frozen Master-Sequential LinUCB heuristic selects per-UAV exit depths using calibrated confidence, local compute, transmission, and synchronization delays.","l":[[7,"III.D Online Inference: Master-Sequential LinUCB Routing","reward is computed to reflect prediction correctness"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0075","key":"outcomes","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Combining Jetson TX2 profiling with simulated Rician wireless links, CIDER trades slight accuracy for lower routing-controlled latency; sensitivity tests vary scale and rate.","l":[[10,"IV.B Results Analysis","establishes the empirical upper bounds for inference accuracy"]],"g":null}
{"id":"R0075","key":"partition_assignment","s":"OBSERVED","f":"Ranks teacher feature channels by activation strength and assigns them to student UAVs by compute capability with deterministic boundary overlap.","l":[[4,"III.C Offline Training: Multi-Exit Feature Alignment","partitioned across student models according to"]],"g":null}
